From: GameShellNeo development <gameshellneo@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] PM: wakeup: preserve managed initialization errors

Do not register a managed disable action when wakeup initialization failed.
Otherwise the wrapper reports the action-registration result instead of the
initial error, and its later cleanup can disable an existing wakeup source.

Keep device_init_wakeup() capability behavior and the add-action-or-reset
failure path unchanged.

---
 include/linux/pm_wakeup.h | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/pm_wakeup.h b/include/linux/pm_wakeup.h
--- a/include/linux/pm_wakeup.h
+++ b/include/linux/pm_wakeup.h
@@ -238,7 +238,12 @@ static void device_disable_wakeup(void *dev)
  */
 static inline int devm_device_init_wakeup(struct device *dev)
 {
-	device_init_wakeup(dev, true);
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = device_init_wakeup(dev, true);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	return devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, device_disable_wakeup, dev);
 }
 
